WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.260
Can Donkey Kong Jr.

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:03.860
save his papa from Mario's prison?

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:26.940
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:28.500
I'm Mike. And I'm Sean.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:33.100
And it's just the two of us for the rest of the Donkey Kong ride.

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:39.360
For some reason, our other castmates don't really want to talk about Donkey Kong.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.400
They don't like Donkey Kong.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.860
I want to get off Donkey Kong Wild Ride.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.440
I don't want to be on it anymore.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:51.220
I don't know. Mario has now gone insane and has set up a prison.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.080
Yeah. But you know what?

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:56.300
Something I want to talk about real fast before we even...

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.000
I assume people are familiar.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.400
We will talk about the objective.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.980
But where does this game take place?

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:07.860
This game takes place in Mario's sub-

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:12.260
sub-Turanean Brooklyn dungeon.

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:13.900
It's like the jungle.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:20.140
It's the jungle, but also like a weird like technologically advanced area.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:23.280
And you know what I'm talking about, right?

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:24.360
Yeah, I do know what you're talking about. Yeah.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:25.400
It's incredibly strange.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:28.400
And also, Mario captured Donkey Kong, right?

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:30.940
Because he doesn't like animals or whatever.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:33.060
That's his pet animal or whatever.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.340
Right? He's captured him as like a form of punishment.

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:37.200
But then he's releasing animals.

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:40.420
Yeah. Like half, just face crocodiles.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.060
Just the faces of the crocodiles.

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:45.700
And he's releasing them at Donkey Kong Jr.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:46.920
So it's like...

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:48.420
I mean, that means to an end.

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:52.860
Anyway, I think we need to talk a little bit about how we usually do this.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:54.780
Because if this is your first episode, I'm sorry.

00:01:55.100 --> 00:02:00.560
Second off, if this is your first episode, please listen to like Super Mario Brothers or Donkey Kong.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.440
Before you... You can't just come in Donkey Kong Jr.

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:04.620
Yeah, this isn't fair to us.

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:08.080
Yeah, this is improper. Anyway, let's do first impressions.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:21.860
Yeah. Yeah, what do you got?

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:28.240
Okay. So I think that my first impression was like, okay, this is a pretty cool way to do a sequel.

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:32.340
It's not an improvement at all.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:33.740
On the first game.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:37.140
But at least it wasn't just like, all right, let's just do more levels.

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:39.600
Yeah. It was an actual like...

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:41.140
It was something novel.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:42.260
It was something new.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:48.320
But it was not as fun or as memorable as Donkey Kong.

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:52.600
Yeah. I think for me, the first impression, even like my...

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:54.520
I remember my very first impression of Donkey Kong Jr.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:58.160
Was just like, this is really strange that Mario...

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:00.600
Like, you know, because I mean, you know, it's not my first game.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.160
Like, I knew Mario before.

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:03.360
So this is like really strange.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:04.420
Mario's the villain.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:06.480
Donkey Kong is locked up.

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:08.680
So you're forced to play as Donkey Kong Jr.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:14.820
And if there's one thing I'll reward this game for, it is that they, you know, the first

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:19.760
game kind of defines platform games with its ability to jump over obstacles and land on

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:20.620
platforms and stuff like that.

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:23.520
This one, it finds a totally different way to do the platforming.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:26.860
And I just think that's got to be appreciated a little bit.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:32.360
Like, I definitely thought that it was neat that they didn't just do another like, oh, Donkey Kong's

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:33.920
escaped and this time it's harder.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:43.660
Yeah, exactly. Like, I think that the introduction of vines or whatever they use in the later levels...

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:44.980
Yeah. Chains.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:47.160
Yeah. At one point, there's just chains.

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:52.900
And like, there's actually some mechanical depth to them too in that you can decide whether

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:54.460
you want to hold on to one or two.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:56.300
Right. To go fast or slow.

00:03:56.860 --> 00:03:59.280
But also be more open to attacks.

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:01.360
Or just obstacles, I mean.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:05.000
While we're on the subject too of like where they could have taken this game, imagine if

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:07.420
it was like, oh, you thought Donkey Kong was bad?

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:09.060
Wait till you see Donkey Kong Jr.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:10.400
And they made Donkey Kong Jr.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:11.900
the villain. Like the psychopath.

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:17.560
Right? Like, he's the new villain and Mario is now has to like, Donkey Kong Jr.'s even worse.

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:19.780
You know? It's like, they could have done that.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:21.820
They could have. Yeah. I'm glad that they didn't do that either.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:25.080
I'm glad that you actually play as Donkey Kong in this one.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:26.560
Well, Donkey Kong Jr. Yeah.

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:29.700
So, I guess we'll go through the objective real fast.

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:31.040
It seems pretty obvious at this point.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:34.980
Mario has stolen, has kidnapped, prisoned.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:39.720
I don't know. It's like, he's done the same thing that happened to his girlfriend Pauline in the first one.

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:42.980
And now he's like, I'm going to lock up Donkey Kong Jr., him who's boss.

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:43.980
You know what I think happened?

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:47.180
I think that Pauline has left Mario.

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:50.900
And this is his way of taking it out on Donkey Kong.

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:51.980
He's lashing it on Donkey Kong.

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:57.880
But apparently, sometime between Donkey Kong and Donkey Kong Jr., Donkey Kong had a girlfriend

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:01.820
or a wife or something and gave birth to Donkey Kong Jr.

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:03.120
And Donkey Kong Jr.

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:06.580
is pretty pissed that Mario imprisoned his dad.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:10.840
So he's going to try and save him from that by collecting keys.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:13.740
Which is only really obvious in the final level.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:19.340
Yeah. In the other ones, it's just like the key is directly at the part where the level would usually end anyway.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:21.300
Well, I think, yeah, you're right.

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:22.800
You don't associate it with collecting the key.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.140
You just associate it with getting to the end of the stage.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:28.700
Yeah. It would be interesting if the key was at like a different part of the level, but it's not.

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:31.160
No. So it's very similar to Donkey Kong.

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:35.540
Instead, you're just going from point A to the top of the levels.

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:39.460
This way you can get to the key and open and free Donkey Kong.

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:45.980
However, Mario just like immediately seals him up again and takes him to the next part.

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:51.180
This Groundhog Day nightmare situation where everything that you do just gets wiped out and maybe you have to do it again.

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:54.640
But I think it's funny that...

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:55.520
It's not funny at all.

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:56.560
It's not funny.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:59.740
Nothing is funny about an ape being imprisoned.

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:02.680
Okay? I don't want PETA on us.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:19.220
Okay. I like how they kept the blueprint of the level progression the same between Donkey Kong and Donkey Kong Jr.

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:27.360
You've got three levels of varying difficulty and mechanical enhancement, I guess.

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:32.880
And then the third one is like that it's kind of a set piece, if you can call it that.

00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:38.340
In the first one, you had to get all of the weak points of the structure.

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:44.960
And in this one, you have to get all of the keys up the string or whatever.

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:46.040
Up the chain, I think it is.

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:51.140
Where it's like you have all these separate objectives before you actually can do the main one.

00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:59.860
Yeah. And as you were alluding to with the gameplay, it is cool how you go up one branch or whatever you want to call them.

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:00.860
One tree vine.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:03.560
And you go kind of slow.

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:09.900
But if you kind of extend yourself between both of them, if you hold on to two vines, you can go up kind of fast.

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:13.220
But then you risk getting hit by one.

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:14.660
Or a bird will hit you.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:19.580
Right. And there's some good enemies in this one, better than the barrels and fire in Donkey Kong.

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:25.600
This one has the crocodiles that just like have a one way path between, you know, they're very easy to avoid.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:30.420
The birds are a little tedious because they'll kind of be directly above you.

00:07:30.520 --> 00:07:31.920
But then they also drop those eggs.

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:38.810
Oh, yeah. And they seem to when they when they make a turnaround, they seem to just go on whatever level you're currently on.

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:43.910
Yeah. So if you are on like halfway through the stage, it'll meet you at halfway through the stage.

00:07:44.050 --> 00:07:45.750
So then you either choose to climb up or climb down.

00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:47.290
Nothing that's like cheap.

00:07:47.510 --> 00:07:50.670
Yeah. But it is all about the weaponization of animals.

00:07:50.890 --> 00:07:52.530
Yeah. Throwing animals at you.

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:54.210
Yeah. And then later electricity.

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:55.610
Yeah. For some reason.

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:57.270
Yeah. I don't really know the story.

00:07:57.390 --> 00:07:59.970
I mean, like we can go level by level if you want.

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:08.830
The first one is, I guess, just like an introduction where the beginning is kind of boring and you're just moving across platforms.

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:15.630
Yeah. And then you get to go on to the you get to test out that those new features with the with the vines.

00:08:16.070 --> 00:08:22.290
And is it the second one or is it the third one where you go into you go into Tron land?

00:08:22.510 --> 00:08:23.650
No, that's the third one.

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:28.810
So the second one has the has the weird like yellow.

00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:29.850
Oh, yeah.

00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:34.970
Sponge like things that move on the platforms that like you jump on to and then they drop you a little bit.

00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:37.490
Yeah. But otherwise, they look like they're unreachable.

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:39.430
It's not great design.

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:40.610
It's definitely different.

00:08:41.190 --> 00:08:48.210
And again, it's one of those things where like the difficulty between the first level and the second level is definitely a big ramp.

00:08:48.450 --> 00:08:51.470
So this way it's like, hey, that was just to teach you how to play the game.

00:08:51.850 --> 00:08:52.790
Now that you know how to play.

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:53.990
Give us all your quarters.

00:08:54.270 --> 00:09:00.470
Yeah, die. But if you were lucky enough to get through the second level, which again, like these games aren't hard.

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:01.630
They're easy to be beat.

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:10.710
But if once you get to that second level, the third level is like the Tron world you were alluding to where it's like the electricity stuff going by.

00:09:10.710 --> 00:09:12.550
But it's not hard.

00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:21.590
It's not hard. It's just it's just if anything, the thing that I found myself like stupidly getting killed on was I would see the blue guy coming really fast down the way.

00:09:21.710 --> 00:09:23.690
And I'd be like, oh, I got to jump over him.

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:25.530
And then I get hit by the guy above me.

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:27.770
I wouldn't even be looking at anything else.

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:29.170
I'd just be focusing on the blue guy.

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:31.550
So that's just like it's a dumb way to lose a quarter.

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:35.190
So I'm glad that I have the NES version to save me from.

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:37.470
But then again, spending any more money on this game.

00:09:37.650 --> 00:09:44.590
One thing we didn't talk about is so let's say these games were probably like, what, 40 bucks, somewhere around there, somewhere around 40 bucks.

00:09:44.690 --> 00:09:46.290
Right. In in 1986.

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:48.190
Yeah. How many quarters?

00:09:48.390 --> 00:09:51.650
Like, that's a lot of quarters in order for this game to be worth it.

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:54.210
Yeah. Instead of just going to the time to play Dungeon Jr.

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:57.150
Oh, wow. I guess like a hundred.

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:03.150
I think that would be if it was $25, Mike.

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:04.830
But it's somewhere between.

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:07.850
