00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:09.910
I just figured you have to play it a lot.

00:10:10.030 --> 00:10:11.030
Like, you have to really like it.

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:13.970
Yeah. You have to really like this game for it to be worth it.

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:16.590
But there's like, you know, there's a rate of return on this game, which is great.

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:20.850
You can't say the same for other games that didn't get the arcade port treatment.

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:27.290
Mm hmm. But at that point, at this point in Nintendo's lifespan, everything pretty much has a arcade

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:29.330
game except for Gyromite and Stack Up.

00:10:29.570 --> 00:10:30.890
Oh, God. Don't bring that up.

00:10:31.010 --> 00:10:34.370
Yeah. I'm sorry. I thought we were done with Rob, but we're never done with Rob.

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:36.250
We're never done with Rob. OK.

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:37.770
So that's the Tron world.

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:41.590
Yeah. And just because I feel like we kind of talked about that one real fast.

00:10:41.690 --> 00:10:42.670
You're dodging electricity.

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:44.470
And there's like these. It's very simple.

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:48.570
Very simple stages because it's just bars that you go up from one side to the other.

00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:52.550
The only notable thing about that level is just how out of place it seems.

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:57.050
Yeah. It's almost like he brought him, you know, like he took him to the jungle and then was

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:57.910
like, wait, real fast.

00:10:58.530 --> 00:10:59.710
Like, come back.

00:10:59.850 --> 00:11:01.550
