00:13:22.930 --> 00:13:25.350
Yeah, I have some straight thoughts about this game.

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:35.070
One is forget that we just talked about how random it is that you're now Dunyong Jr.

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:36.650
and you got to do all that stuff.

00:13:37.010 --> 00:13:38.970
My straight thought isn't my own.

00:13:38.970 --> 00:13:45.670
It's actually coming from Miyamoto in an interview he did with Nintendo Magazine in the UK.

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:48.330
Is this going to be another one of those very vague things?

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:53.290
No, because unlike Sakamoto, who I was trying to mention did the pixel art for this game,

00:13:53.410 --> 00:13:57.350
or at least some of it, which again, Sakamoto, if you don't know, he's the Metroid guy.

00:13:57.650 --> 00:13:59.510
Pretty much the guy who's responsible for Metroid.

00:13:59.510 --> 00:14:04.190
And he did some other stuff for the NES launch games that we talked about, like Wrecking Crew.

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:06.950
He was the designer behind that and stuff like that.

00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:10.390
So he gives really weird quotes.

00:14:10.650 --> 00:14:15.390
But Miyamoto here actually gives some good insight into the making of Dunyong Jr.

00:14:15.530 --> 00:14:17.330
here when they talk to him.

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:18.970
So he says, Yes.

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:23.830
During Dunyong's development, we were already thinking about things that would become DK Jr.

00:14:23.830 --> 00:14:25.670
and even designing the stages.

00:14:25.970 --> 00:14:29.930
We had fleshed out all of these ideas, but we couldn't use them in Dunyong.

00:14:30.230 --> 00:14:32.970
So one of my friends who was making the game with me said,

00:14:33.150 --> 00:14:34.330
We've got all these ideas.

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:36.030
Why don't we make another game?

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:38.590
And Nintendo told me to make a sequel to Dunyong.

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:42.010
So I wanted Dunyong to be the player character in this game.

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:43.770
But he is really big.

00:14:44.630 --> 00:14:48.770
So it's like the first mention of Nintendo in really big.

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:51.210
You know people want Ridley and Smash and it's like,

00:14:51.270 --> 00:14:52.550
Oh, he's too big. You know?

00:14:52.730 --> 00:14:54.550
It's like, this is the first really big.

00:14:54.670 --> 00:14:56.770
People are like, Dunyong in the arcade.

00:14:56.970 --> 00:14:58.110
And they're like, Too big.

00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:00.450
They're like, Okay, what about Ridley?

00:15:00.550 --> 00:15:03.050
No. Too big. He's really big.

00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:05.890
So we couldn't really do an action game with him.

00:15:06.010 --> 00:15:08.930
We couldn't make the screen scroll or anything.

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:10.010
And so we thought,

00:15:10.310 --> 00:15:13.410
Well, let's make a little Dunyong to use in place of Mario.

00:15:13.770 --> 00:15:16.510
We did still want a big Dunyong on top of the screen.

00:15:16.530 --> 00:15:18.750
But of course, he couldn't be the main enemy.

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:22.050
It couldn't be the son versus the father.

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:23.190
So we thought,

00:15:23.450 --> 00:15:25.210
Ah, Mario has captured him.

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:28.790
That is such a weird way to come about that.

00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:30.410
I love it. And you know what, though?

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:31.650
Like, we were questioning it all.

00:15:31.750 --> 00:15:33.230
But don't you feel a little better now that you know?

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:34.810
Yeah, I guess so.

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:37.250
There's a little bit of me that feels better now.

00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:40.690
But they push on. The magazine pushes on and says,

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:42.410
What exactly were you thinking?

00:15:42.410 --> 00:15:44.550
Switching the good guy and bad guy.

00:15:45.050 --> 00:15:46.410
When you've talked about Dunyong elsewhere,

00:15:46.410 --> 00:15:48.830
you've said that he was not a bad character.

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:51.590
That maybe he was just misguided or confused.

00:15:51.790 --> 00:15:53.470
I mean, yeah, he's a gorilla.

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:57.570
You know, like, he doesn't have thoughts.

00:15:57.850 --> 00:15:58.950
Like, when he stole Pauline.

00:15:58.950 --> 00:16:00.190
You don't know that, Mike.

00:16:00.190 --> 00:16:02.090
When he stole Pauline, he had no idea what he was doing.

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:10.350
Okay? So Miyamoto answers that, you know, in a way that will shock no one if you're familiar with Miyamoto's affinity for Popeye.

00:16:10.690 --> 00:16:13.530
Okay? He wanted to make Donkey Kong a Popeye game.

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:15.090
We talked about that last week's episode.

00:16:15.430 --> 00:16:17.190
Eventually, he does get to make a Popeye game.

00:16:17.270 --> 00:16:18.790
But at this time, he still couldn't make one.

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:20.030
They wouldn't give him the rights to it.

00:16:20.230 --> 00:16:22.390
So he goes, Yeah, it's like Popeye.

00:16:22.850 --> 00:16:26.470
At that time, I was originally supposed to be making a Popeye-licensed game.

00:16:26.470 --> 00:16:31.930
But when that fell through, I was still thinking about the relationship between Popeye, Bluto, and Olive Oil.

00:16:32.250 --> 00:16:34.430
Their relationship is somewhat friendly.

00:16:34.690 --> 00:16:36.890
They're not enemies. They're friendly rivals.

00:16:37.110 --> 00:16:38.530
But I needed different characters.

00:16:38.770 --> 00:16:42.190
The main character, the big strong guy, and the beautiful woman.

00:16:42.650 --> 00:16:45.530
Well, Olive really isn't a beautiful woman.

00:16:45.670 --> 00:16:47.730
And he just goes on a whole tangent.

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:49.950
Oh my god. He goes on a whole tangent about Popeye.

00:16:50.090 --> 00:16:52.990
And completely, like, disregards the question for the most part.

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:55.810
And it's kind of insulting anybody that may have been attracted to Olive.

00:16:55.810 --> 00:16:59.770
Right, but then when he gets his thoughts back together, Miyamoto fleshes it out with, like,

00:17:00.390 --> 00:17:04.210
What's kind of a mystery is, why did I title the game Donkey Kong?

00:17:04.410 --> 00:17:07.790
The main character, the player, was Mario.

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:09.750
That much was decided.

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:13.470
But really, Donkey Kong's personality was the most fleshed out of them all.

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:18.410
So I really think it's best to name a game after its strongest character.

00:17:18.810 --> 00:17:21.310
Wow. So he thinks Donkey Kong Jr.

00:17:21.370 --> 00:17:24.270
is Donkey Kong Jr.'s strongest character.

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:28.330
I feel like maybe he didn't know what he was talking about during that interview.

00:17:28.350 --> 00:17:29.990
He just got so distracted by Popeye.

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:31.990
I kind of want to talk to Miyamoto about Popeye.

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:35.730
Yeah. You know, because that's a game that we'll be doing very soon.

00:17:35.870 --> 00:17:37.190
The Popeye episode is coming up.

00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:40.110
And it seems like that's all he ever wanted.

00:17:40.270 --> 00:17:41.490
That's all he ever thinks about.

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:45.310
It's weird to think that Nintendo didn't just buy the rights to Popeye at this point.

00:17:45.550 --> 00:17:48.370
Like, they have enough money, they can probably buy the rights to Popeye.

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:51.510
So that's the strayest thought.

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:54.570
That's got to be the strayest thought because we didn't get any answers.

00:17:54.570 --> 00:17:56.810
I set it up like we were going to get answers.

00:17:56.990 --> 00:18:03.530
And really, to this day, no one knows why Mario is the villain in this game.

00:18:03.530 --> 00:18:06.710
Other than the idea of like, you know, whatever.

00:18:06.910 --> 00:18:09.830
It doesn't matter because at that point, Mario wasn't a big deal to us.

00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:13.070
Like, obviously, Mario is not going to be the villain in Mario Party 11.

00:18:13.350 --> 00:18:14.490
I mean, that'd be cool.

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:16.450
Would be pretty cool if you're listening, Nintendo.

00:18:17.390 --> 00:18:18.590
And call into the show.

00:18:19.090 --> 00:18:24.490
Please. One other thing I wanted to talk about is the character, Donkey Kong Jr.

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:26.230
He's like lost to time now.

00:18:26.350 --> 00:18:30.510
Oh, yeah. I mean, I feel like maybe he sort of evolved into Diddy Kong.

00:18:30.910 --> 00:18:32.470
Okay, so no.

00:18:34.190 --> 00:18:36.490
No, I do know a little more than that.

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:39.190
Okay. What's interesting is there's two theories right now.

00:18:39.330 --> 00:18:40.810
Okay. So for what it's worth.

00:18:41.270 --> 00:18:42.310
So you got two theories.

00:18:42.570 --> 00:18:47.410
Yeah. Donkey Kong Jr.'s last game was Mario Tennis on the N64.

00:18:47.990 --> 00:18:49.570
Okay. Oh, that's it.

00:18:49.610 --> 00:18:50.670
That's his last appearance.

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:53.090
Okay. I would have thought that Donkey Kong Jr.

00:18:53.290 --> 00:18:54.310
Math was his last. Yeah.

00:18:54.350 --> 00:18:55.810
No, no, no. So he appears in Donkey Kong Jr.

00:18:56.010 --> 00:19:01.090
Math. He appears in Super Mario Kart, a game that Donkey Kong does not appear in.

00:19:01.510 --> 00:19:02.430
Okay. Donkey Kong Jr.

00:19:02.550 --> 00:19:04.110
is in that game, but not Donkey Kong.

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:11.190
Donkey Kong Country screws everything up because Donkey Kong Country establishes that Cranky

00:19:11.190 --> 00:19:13.650
Kong is the original Donkey Kong.

00:19:14.050 --> 00:19:17.710
Whoa. And that the Donkey Kong in that game is his grandson.

00:19:18.330 --> 00:19:20.290
Okay. Donkey Kong Jr.'s son.

00:19:21.790 --> 00:19:25.670
Right. But then in Donkey Kong Country 2, in the manual,

00:19:25.670 --> 00:19:32.330
Donkey Kong, Cranky Kong is the narrator of the manual and keeps referring to Donkey Kong

00:19:32.330 --> 00:19:37.370
in that game as his son, which would make Donkey Kong Jr.

00:19:37.730 --> 00:19:40.190
the current day Donkey Kong, which

00:19:40.190 --> 00:19:42.790
would be fine because Donkey Kong Jr.

00:19:42.790 --> 00:19:44.810
would have evolved into Donkey Kong.

00:19:45.170 --> 00:19:50.070
Right. And Cranky Kong was the old Donkey Kong.

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:51.070
This is so stupid.

00:19:51.170 --> 00:19:52.430
It all makes sense when you think about it.

00:19:52.530 --> 00:19:53.750
But here's where things get crazy.

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:54.990
What was his last?

00:19:55.070 --> 00:19:56.650
What was Donkey Kong Jr.'s last game?

00:19:57.190 --> 00:19:58.970
Mario Tennis on the N64.

00:19:58.970 --> 00:20:01.830
A game that features Donkey Kong.

00:20:03.630 --> 00:20:10.350
But this is the same game that has Mario and Baby Mario in it as well.

00:20:10.530 --> 00:20:12.230
So I don't think we can take that for canon.

00:20:12.510 --> 00:20:15.210
And I think I'm going to go ahead and put Donkey Kong Jr.

00:20:15.350 --> 00:20:17.810
as a 100% lock as the character

00:20:17.810 --> 00:20:19.630
you play as in Donkey Kong Country.

00:20:20.070 --> 00:20:23.250
Wow. So the Donkey Kong we know today is Donkey Kong Jr.

00:20:23.590 --> 00:20:25.250
and the Donkey Kong from the arcade

00:20:25.830 --> 00:20:26.850
is Cranky Kong.

00:20:27.030 --> 00:20:30.030
I don't like that idea, but I'll concede it.

00:20:30.270 --> 00:20:31.630
What would you prefer? Donkey Kong Jr.'s dead?

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:33.790
No, I would just prefer...

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:36.090
Yes. And who is Cranky Kong?

00:20:36.570 --> 00:20:37.590
Cranky Kong just...

00:20:37.590 --> 00:20:38.710
He's... Donkey Kong's dead.

00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:39.890
But like the...

00:20:39.890 --> 00:20:41.250
Is he the arcade Donkey Kong?

00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:42.990
No, no. Donkey Kong is Donkey Kong.

00:20:43.150 --> 00:20:44.630
Okay, so Donkey Kong has always been Donkey Kong.

00:20:44.810 --> 00:20:45.670
Everyone... No one ages.

00:20:46.090 --> 00:20:47.990
No, but like it's not like...

00:20:47.990 --> 00:20:51.130
It's not like the Green Lantern where it just...

00:20:51.130 --> 00:20:52.890
Where it changes all the time.

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:55.570
Right, right. Like why would his name be Cranky Kong?

00:20:55.770 --> 00:20:57.690
Like it's like, oh, you're over a certain age now.

00:20:57.770 --> 00:20:58.670
You're Cranky Kong. Now you're Cranky.

00:20:58.910 --> 00:21:05.250
Yeah. Another thing, since we're talking about ages here, how old do you think Mario is in Donkey

00:21:05.250 --> 00:21:06.510
Kong, the arcade game?

00:21:06.650 --> 00:21:09.090
And Donkey Kong Jr. for that matter, since they're like direct sequels.

00:21:09.090 --> 00:21:12.550
Well, I kind of think he's ageless and he's always just been him.

00:21:12.550 --> 00:21:13.990
If you had to put an age on him.

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:15.830
40. 40, right?

00:21:15.970 --> 00:21:18.270
Yeah. Miyamoto like laughs about that.

00:21:18.410 --> 00:21:20.770
He can't believe that we think he's so old.

00:21:20.890 --> 00:21:23.530
He's like, that guy, he looks like he's in his 20s.

00:21:24.710 --> 00:21:28.790
He imagined Mario to just be like this bachelor living in Brooklyn.

00:21:29.330 --> 00:21:30.230
That's so strange. In his 20s.

00:21:30.530 --> 00:21:35.390
I'm like, nah man, you know, with the overalls and the mustache and the hat and the fact that

00:21:35.390 --> 00:21:39.150
he's a plumber, you really didn't set him up to be like any younger than 40.

00:21:39.330 --> 00:21:44.690
Yeah. Maybe in the maybe if he made this game in the 70s, like that raises concerns, though,

00:21:44.850 --> 00:21:51.030
about like a man in his 40s kidnapping a giant ape and then being chased after by his like

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:53.610
son. Is that that's more concerning?

00:21:53.930 --> 00:21:55.890
I just think it's concerning that a 40 year old.

00:21:56.110 --> 00:21:59.430
Well, it would be I guess it would be a little more concerning if it was a 20 year old doing

00:21:59.430 --> 00:22:03.350
nothing better to do. Like he's got Pauline, but he's like, no, I gotta take care of this girl right now.

00:22:03.350 --> 00:22:04.990
I just need to do this.

00:22:05.110 --> 00:22:10.250
Well, I guess what all we're all we're really saying is that this this entire franchise makes

00:22:10.250 --> 00:22:15.610
no sense. Yeah, this is this is I'm almost glad that the young country is like the more established

00:22:15.610 --> 00:22:19.690
thing. Yeah. And that the arcade games are just like we wanted money.

00:22:21.310 --> 00:22:26.530
So I think like one thing that we need to do now is the essential games list.

